Wait — should the in-flight check lock the in-flight plan row? Yes, lockPlan for update to serialize with concurrent checkins etc. Good.

Note: plan_no uniqueness — use nextPlanNoSequence with "T" prefix.

Duplicate temp same day: the unique constraint (atm, date, type) also protects concurrency — catch DuplicateKeyException → treat as "当日已存在临时计划" item? In concurrent generation with distinct requestIds, second insert throws DuplicateKeyException which would roll back the whole transaction. Better to catch and return item not-generated. But catching DuplicateKeyException inside a transaction in H2 — after a constraint violation, can the transaction continue? In H2, a failed statement doesn't abort the whole transaction (unlike PostgreSQL). The existing code does exactly this in createPlan (catches DuplicateKeyException and throws BusinessException → rollback). For forecast, catching and continuing with other ATMs... the existing createPlan catches and throws, so transaction rolls back. For per-ATM continue, catching DuplicateKeyException and continuing is what the existing pattern suggests is OK in H2 (insertPlan javadoc says "便于服务层在同一事务内捕获并继续"). I'll catch DuplicateKeyException around insertPlan and add item "当日已存在临时计划，不重复生成".

